WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.870
The UN has 193 member states.

2
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.510
Yet it is not a world government.

3
00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:12.030
Its Charter was signed in San
Francisco, on 26 June 1945.

4
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:18.190
From 1948, a General Agreement on Tariffs
and Trade set rules for world trade.

5
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.910
So who makes the rules that hold
the global economy together?

6
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.650
The richest country alone?

7
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.450
Or nobody at all?

8
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.390
In this mission, you'll trace how an
unwritten expectation can harden into written

9
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.850
rules, step by step.

10
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.330
Then you'll weigh who
gains from these rules,

11
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:38.950
from the global scale right
down to local councils.

12
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.550
Your mission: find out who makes
the rules of the global economy,

13
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.280
and who they serve.
